      "nets": ["+5V", "NET0031 (I2C_SDA)", "NET0046 (I2C_SCL)", "GND"],
      "observed": "The schematic shows the LiDAR interface PR2 connected through P8: VCC to +5V, SDA/SCL to the main I2C nets, and GND to ground. Those I2C nets connect to ESP32 IO4/IO5.",
      "expected": "The specification says the TF-Luna LiDAR is unwired, with its pins free, and describes water-level ranging as an HC-SR04-style sensor on GPIO4/GPIO5. The schematic instead provides a powered I2C LiDAR interface and no separate trigger/echo interface.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "PR2 LiDAR; P8 pins VCC, SDA, SCL, GND connect to +5V, NET0031, NET0046, and GND; page 1/1."
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "ESP32 IO4/I2C_SDA is NET0031 and IO5/I2C_SCL is NET0046; page 1/1."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "The r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no ... and all four pins ... typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "The firmware ... defines an ultrasonic platform sensor ... trigger_pin: GPIO4, echo_pin: GPIO5."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The water-level sensor interface shown on the board does not match the specified HC-SR04 trigger/echo interface. A LiDAR module using this connector would use I2C instead, so the specified ultrasonic sensor cannot be connected as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.76
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic wires a LiDAR interface to +5V and the main I2C bus, while the specification describes the LiDAR as unwired and the water-level ranging interface as trigger/echo GPIO. This is a substantive mismatch in the water-level sensor interface."
}

